load-balancer-selection is the vendor-neutral load-balancing and application-delivery (ADC) DESIGN and
platform-selection umbrella: which layer to balance at (L4 vs L7), which proxy model fits the traffic
(full-proxy / transparent / DSR), which algorithm and persistence method the application needs, where
TLS terminates, and which platform earns the deployment. It is the design-and-selection entry point for
the load-balancer family; per-vendor configuration and operations live in the sibling skills
(haproxy-load-balancing, nginx-load-balancing, aws-load-balancing), which land in PR 2 of this family.
Skill licensed MIT (the primary-source licence).

Scope + cadence (decided with the user at plan time, 2026-06-18 AskUserQuestion):
  - Naming = scope-explicit: umbrella `load-balancer-selection` + `haproxy-load-balancing` +
    `nginx-load-balancing` + `aws-load-balancing`.
  - PR cadence = two PRs: PR 1 = this umbrella; PR 2 = the three vendor ops skills.
  - Vendor-skill scope = full ops (architecture + config + best-practices/ops + diagnostics) per the
    DNS-family precedent, since there are no pre-existing load-balancer diagnostic skills to route to.
  - This umbrella owns DESIGN / ARCHITECTURE-SELECTION / PLATFORM-COMPARISON only; per-vendor
    configuration is routed out via "When not to use" to the three vendor skills.

